From 0102585905621b7d5a99e509d9240636b304ddce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 22:33:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] ci: stop committing a version stamp the deploy overwrites
 anyway
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Five data jobs ran ./bump-version.sh and committed index.html,
service-worker.js and version.json alongside their data. deploy-pages.yml
rewrites all of it inside _site/ on every deploy — ?v=, APP_VERSION,
CACHE_NAME, version.json and the _formatWindow snapshot (its "Cache-bust
asset references" step) — so the committed stamp never reaches a user.

What it did instead: ~147 commits a month touching the 845 KB index.html, and
a new service-worker CACHE_NAME several times a day, which makes the activate
handler wipe every client's cache on each visit.

bump-version.sh stays for humans changing js/css/index.html by hand, exactly
as CLAUDE.md describes. Only the data jobs stop calling it.

weekly-full-update needed no git-add change (it uses `git add -A`, and with
the bump gone those three files simply no longer differ).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Ld5WCR1Wjb95tBgocvSXbH
